
          -- Zeus Bulletin Board System - Version 1.2 History --

o Added some new options to CLIDoor:

    CLRON               - Enable screen clears while user is in door
    CLROFF              - Disable screen clears...
    STATUS '"<string>"' - Set the status string

o Fixed some serious memory problems in zapp.device.

o The SDCMD_SETPARAMS command wasn't working properly in zapp.device
  (depending on what serial device was in use).

o Removed CR character at the end of the 'Dialing ....' ZMailer window
  status string.

o Changed all ZMailer CMD_RESETs to CMD_CLEARs.  CMD_RESET caused
  8n1.device to divide by zero!!

o Cleaned up ZMPs interactive hatch IO.

o ZMPs AreaFix now generates MSGID kludges in its replies.

o Rewrote and speeded up ZGate's code to do with converting InterNet news
  and mail to fido packets.

o Drastically speeded up ZGate when writing its index files to disk.

o Added MIME detection into ZGate.

o In ZMP you can now have several NETEXEC commands with the same name but
  different passwords.

o Optimized the ZAPP packet receive routine.

o Added MIN and MAX arguments to Zeus:Bin/BM to set the minimum/maximum
  access levels when adding bulletins.

o When adding a bulletin, max access was set to zero instead of 255 -
  fixed!

o If ANSI or RIP are run and that line already has a watcher running, it
  will be uniconified.

o The RIP watcher was opening pipes with the wrong names!  This caused it
  not to work at all!!

o ZGate now removes any Origin or --- lines from fido messages.

o Fixed minor ANSI bug which could cause crashes on some (very rare) ANSI
  codes.

o The command line history list wasn't being reset when calling ResetEdit().

o ZMailer now takes a new command line argument (SHOW/S) to make it open
  its window on startup.

o ZMailer now selects the correct address with systems using YooHoo and
  FTSC-1.

o Fixed time remaining problem when using MaxMinsPerDay and MaxMinsPerCall.

o ZMP now strips trailing spaces from AreaFix commands.

o This version of ZAPP is not totally compatible with previous releases...

o Finally found a bug that may have been causing CLIDoor to crash if it
  couldn't load the door.

o Expanded the ZSegs structure to include a BPTR of the directory where
  the program was found.  Will be set to NULL if it was a resident program.

o CLIDoors and ZDoors now have their pr_HomeDir and pr_CurrentDir setup
  correctly!

o ZDOOR now takes a DIR argument like CLIDoor to set the working directory.

